  "title": "Absolute paths in link labels and link titles are not rewritten",
  "detail": "The link pattern consumes the whole Markdown link, but the callback only rewrites the destination; when the destination is unchanged it returns the original match. So '[' + W + '/a.ts](src/a.ts)' and '[f](src/a.ts \"See ' + W + '/a.ts\")' are published unchanged, and so is an absolute-path label on an https destination. Rewrite paths in the label and the optional title as well as the destination, while leaving ordinary relative and web destinations alone. Add tests for each."
 },
