  "detail": "'[f](file://' + W + '/a.ts)' and a bare 'file://' + W + '/a.ts' pass through unchanged, because the bare-path pattern refuses a path preceded by '/' and a link destination starting with file:// doesn't start with a root. Also, the roots are compared only as configured: if the worktree or data directory is reached through a symlink, the realpath spelling that tools and test output print is not rewritten. Treat a file:// URL whose path is under a root like the bare path, and compare against both the configured and the realpath spelling of each root. Percent-encoded and ~-relative spellings are out of scope (the private-strings check blocks them)."
 },
